{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790989036,"nonce":"MWd8siFcUySjstKcvdjs5pnk/Z8=","message":"Text rendering landed in 9c8159e. Input events (keys, text input, click handlers) remain; pointer hover and press already drive hover: and active: through ashui.input.Pointer.\n\nHow it draws: a text node's glyphs are shaped and rasterized by blinc_text at font size x display scale x sqrt|det| of the node's transform, bucketed at 12 steps per doubling and capped at 256px. Glyph quads are snapped to whole device pixels when the transform has no rotation or skew. Atlases are uploaded by revision, so several renderers can share the one engine; when the atlases fill, the frame clears them and rebuilds once.\n\nCompared with Blinc: Blinc folds the transform into the quad and clamps raster size to 6-32px in its immediate path, so zoomed text is a magnified bitmap. In tests/fixtures/render/Pixels.hx, 10px text under a 4x zoom has stem edges 0px wide; with glyphs rasterized at layout size the same check reads 6px.\n\nAlso found: Taffy rounds box sizes to whole pixels, so a text box can come out up to half a pixel narrower than its measured text and the last word wraps. The line breaker gets a 1px allowance.\n\nStill to do here, beyond input:\n- upload only the atlas region that changed (blinc_text exposes no dirty rect, so the whole atlas goes up);\n- subpixel positioning;\n- letter spacing in measurement (Blinc a368d49).","files":null}]}